@* ADR 0279 — the one hand-drawn icon sprite. Rendered once per page by
   _Layout (right after <body>); every nav / account-menu icon is a
   <svg class="kmb-icon"><use href="#kmb-i-…"/></svg> that points here, so an
   icon is drawn in exactly one place (the row nav and the rail used to carry
   two inline copies each).

   Drawing rules (keep new icons in the family):
   - 24×24 grid, outline only; stroke / caps / joins come from the .kmb-icon
     class in site.css (1.75, round, round) — don't set them per symbol.
   - Soft corners (rx 2–3), shapes that stay distinct from every sibling.
   - The "character" accent: small filled dots (and the home heart) echoing
     the dotted K mark. Mark them class="kmb-ico-accent" with the inline
     fill:var(--kmb-icon-accent, currentColor) — <use> shadow trees can't be
     reached by page selectors, but they DO inherit custom properties, so a
     context can tint the accents by setting --kmb-icon-accent.
   - Menu section headings carry no icon; only clickable items do (Per, 2026-10-31).
   IconSpriteTests pins that every referenced id has a symbol here. *@
